!! Short version: do not approve until three things are answered. (1) Does the pump firmware accept 1-decimal mL/h, and was that tested on real hardware or a simulator? (2) Is the vancomycin cap change (80 to 60 mg/kg/day) backed by the P&T approval itself, not a comment about it? (3) How was the gentamicin fixture generated, and does it check the code against anything independent of the code? Green checks only prove the code does what the author's tests say.

