## Where a mistake could hurt a patient

cards
### Pump precision (export.ts)
Rates now go out with 1 decimal. If the firmware accepts 2 and the new code assumes it only needs 1, the pump may run at a slightly different rate than the system calculated. Worst for the lowest rates, which means the smallest patients.
### Rounding direction (round.ts)
Half-up rounds exact halves up every time. Ask whether rounding happens before or after the max cap is applied. If before, a rounded-up dose can land above the cap.
### Vancomycin cap (formulary-overrides.yaml)
The cap drops from 80 to 60 mg/kg/day. Doses ordered above 60 are now clamped or flagged. Ask which, and whether the prescriber and pharmacist can see that it happened. The only evidence of approval is a comment saying P&T approved it on 14 Sep.
### Band edges and per-drug caps (bands.ts, limits.ts)
A child at exactly 3 kg, 10 kg or 25 kg must land in one band only. A drug missing from the per-drug cap table must fail loudly, not fall back to no cap.
### Units (units.ts)
Anything converting mcg to mg that is off by a factor of 1,000 gives a dose that is 1,000 times too small or too large. Check the direction and that it has a test each way.
### The fixture
The gentamicin fixture is 1,120 lines nobody has read, generated from the formulary. If the expected values were produced by the same logic being tested, the tests agree with the code by construction.

## Questions for the author

1. Does the pump firmware accept 1-decimal rates, and was this tested on a pump or only in a simulator? (Tomasz asked; no answer shown.)
2. Why half-up rather than banker's rounding? Is the choice documented, and who signed off on it clinically? (Priya asked.)
3. Is rounding done before or after the max mg/kg/day cap, and can a rounded dose exceed the cap?
4. Is rounding done in floating point? Which function rounds, and what does it do with exact halves and with values like 2.675?
5. Which band do exactly 3, 10 and 25 kg fall into, and is there a test for each edge?
6. What happens to a drug with no per-drug cap entry, and to a weight outside every band, such as 0 or a missing weight?
7. What changes in practice for a patient on vancomycin at 60 to 80 mg/kg/day? Is the prescriber told? Where is the P&T approval record of 14 Sep, not just the comment?
8. Why is there a gentamicin fixture and no vancomycin one, when vancomycin is the drug whose cap changed?
9. How was the gentamicin fixture generated, and from which version of the formulary? Does anything check it independently of the new code?
10. Does round.test.ts include the old 2-decimal behaviour as a comparison, so we can see exactly what shifted?
11. Is there a rollback plan if a ward reports a wrong rate after Thursday?

