- [ ] Open formulary-overrides.yaml and ask for the P&T approval record.
- [ ] Read bands.ts and limits.ts for the edge cases (3, 10, 25 kg; missing drug).
- [ ] Skim round.test.ts for the boundary and exact-half cases only.
- [ ] Sample 5 to 10 rows of the fixture against the formulary, including rows at the band edges.
- [ ] Post the questions above, then request changes or hold approval until the answers arrive.

## Draft note for the St. Brendan's ward champion

The ward champion needs a summary before Thursday. Do not send it until questions 1, 3 and 7 are answered.

- Doses for children are now rounded using new rules per weight band: 0-3 kg, 3-10 kg, 10-25 kg and 25+ kg.
- Pump rates are sent with 1 decimal place instead of 2. Pending confirmation that the pumps accept this.
- The daily maximum dose limit is now set per drug.
- The vancomycin daily maximum goes from 80 to 60 mg/kg/day, per the Pharmacy and Therapeutics approval of 14 Sep. Pending sight of that approval.
- The display label changes from "mL/hr" to "mL/h". Nothing else changes on screen.

## What I could not establish

I have only the file list, notes and comments, not the code. I cannot tell what the old bands were, how the rounding is implemented, or whether the pump accepts 1 decimal. The clinical effect of the vancomycin change is a question for the pharmacist or Dr. Adeyemi-Clarke, not for a developer to judge.
